1643	73	12	9	Data Modeling & Data Warehousing Foundations	{"Day": "Day 9", "Hours": "8", "Difficulty": "⭐⭐⭐⭐", "Session Title": "Data Modeling & Data Warehousing Foundations  🆕 NEW", "Hands-On / Workshop": "Model a banking data mart end to end: draw the ER model, declare the grain, design a star schema for payments analytics (fact_transaction + dim_customer / dim_account / dim_merchant / dim_date), then snowflake one dimension and compare query complexity · write the data dictionary and business metadata for every field · implement the model in SQL and load it from the Day 3–4 transaction data.", "Assessment / Assignment": "Assignment: complete dimensional model for a banking payments mart — ER diagram, star schema, grain statements, SCD strategy, data dictionary and metadata sheet. Scored on grain correctness, key design and metadata completeness.", "Banking Domain Use Case": "Payments data mart — fact_transaction star schema for a private bank", "AI Integration Touchpoint": "Claude generates a first-cut dimensional model from a business description → the learner audits it for wrong grain, missing dimensions, hidden many-to-many relationships and fact-table bloat. Gemini drafts the business metadata.", "Core Topics — Live Session": "NEW MODULE (client feedback) — the foundation the dashboards and pipelines sit on. DATA MODELING: conceptual → logical → physical · ER modelling and cardinality · when to denormalise · dimensional modelling — facts vs dimensions, GRAIN declaration, additive and semi-additive measures · STAR SCHEMA vs SNOWFLAKE SCHEMA and the trade-offs between them · TRANSACTION / fact tables, periodic and accumulating snapshots · slowly-changing dimensions (Type 1/2/3) · surrogate vs natural keys · METADATA — technical, business and operational, data dictionaries, catalogue and lineage. DATA WAREHOUSING: OLTP vs OLAP · Inmon vs Kimball · staging → integration → presentation layers · warehouse vs data lake vs LAKEHOUSE · taught to BOTH tracks (Engineering builds it, the BA reads and challenges it).", "Discipline Thread (Spec-First / Test-First)": "The GRAIN STATEMENT is the spec. No table may be created until the learner has written, in one sentence, exactly what a single row of that table represents — spec-first applied to data design.", "SPL — Self-Paced Topic (not counted in hours)": "Dimensional modelling primer — Kimball star schema, grain, SCD types, metadata and data-dictionary standards"}
1644	73	13	10	Data Engineering, Visualization & Storytelling	{"Day": "Day 10", "Hours": "9", "Difficulty": "⭐⭐⭐⭐", "Session Title": "Data Engineering, Visualization & Storytelling  🆕 ENHANCED", "Hands-On / Workshop": "Build a 3-layer medallion pipeline that lands the Day 9 star schema, with a data-quality gate between each layer · then build the executive dashboard on top of that governed model and deliver a 3-minute narrative to a simulated stakeholder · rebuild one view in Tableau purely to feel the tool difference, then discuss.", "Assessment / Assignment": "Assignment: medallion pipeline + data-quality rule set + a 4-chart executive dashboard built on the governed model, with a 3-minute spoken narrative.", "Banking Domain Use Case": "Banking payments warehouse → leadership dashboard, bronze to boardroom", "AI Integration Touchpoint": "Claude drafts the layer contracts and DQ rule set → the learner audits for missing null, range and referential checks. Gemini drafts the executive narrative, which is then critiqued for wrong emphasis.", "Core Topics — Live Session": "ENHANCED per client feedback — the visualization curriculum now sits on real data-engineering foundations. DATA ENGINEERING: ETL vs ELT and where each belongs · MEDALLION architecture (bronze/silver/gold) · ingestion patterns — full load, incremental, CDC · batch vs streaming · orchestration concepts (DAGs, dependencies, retries, SLAs) · data quality dimensions and validation gates · partitioning and file formats (Parquet/Delta). VISUALIZATION: chart selection and pre-attentive attributes · Power BI report design in depth — drill-through, bookmarks, Performance Analyzer, accessibility · why the model's grain determines what you can slice · Seaborn/Plotly for Python reporting · TABLEAU reviewed against industry relevance and reduced to a 60-minute comparative awareness session. STORYTELLING: Pyramid Principle, SCQA, executive communication, Q&A under pressure.", "Discipline Thread (Spec-First / Test-First)": "Every layer transition needs a written contract — input schema, output schema, the data-quality rules that must pass — before any transformation is written. Chart success criteria are written before the chart is built.", "SPL — Self-Paced Topic (not counted in hours)": "Medallion & lakehouse primer · chart selection cheat-sheet · Power BI performance tuning · Tableau vs Power BI comparison note"}
1645	73	14	11	AI & GenAI Tools Lab — Claude & Gemini	{"Day": "Day 11", "Hours": "8", "Difficulty": "⭐⭐⭐", "Session Title": "AI & GenAI Tools Lab — Claude & Gemini  ⚡ AI Usage Log Starts", "Hands-On / Workshop": "Prompt engineering workshop — 10 prompts for analyst and engineering tasks · run the same banking task through Claude and Gemini and score the outputs side by side · build a personal AI usage playbook.", "Assessment / Assignment": "Document every prompt used and evaluate output quality against a rubric.", "Banking Domain Use Case": "AI-powered competitor analysis for a banking product team", "AI Integration Touchpoint": "Core AI Lab — score accuracy, relevance and hallucination rate for Claude vs Gemini on identical banking tasks.", "Core Topics — Live Session": "TOOL STACK UPDATED per client direction — GitHub Copilot removed. GenAI landscape: capabilities, limitations, hallucinations · prompt engineering — zero-shot, few-shot, chain-of-thought, structured output · CLAUDE for problem framing, spec critique, code and data-model review, long-document reasoning · GEMINI for Workspace-native research, documentation, multimodal work · Claude Code and Gemini Code Assist for repository-aware IDE assistance · context engineering and grounding · model selection — when a reasoning model beats a fast one · AI governance: confidentiality and what must never be pasted into a model", "Discipline Thread (Spec-First / Test-First)": "The AI USAGE LOG becomes a running artefact from today through Day 24 — every AI-assisted output disclosed with the validation evidence beside it.", "SPL — Self-Paced Topic (not counted in hours)": "AI tool landscape primer — Claude & Gemini capability map · AI governance and data-handling rules"}
