1635	73	4	1	Program Kickoff & Banking Domain Immersion	{"Day": "Day 1", "Hours": "8", "Difficulty": "⭐⭐", "Session Title": "Program Kickoff & Banking Domain Immersion  🎯 Discipline Day 1", "Hands-On / Workshop": "Joint workshop: Engineering + MBA learners mixed into pods. Given a Straive banking brief, pods write a problem statement, hypotheses and KPIs together. Individual Scorecard issued and the Day 0 pre-assessment gap analysis reviewed 1:1 with each learner.", "Assessment / Assignment": "Individual: 1-page problem statement + hypothesis tree for an unseen banking case. Scored on clarity, business logic, actionability. Daily tracking begins today — attendance, SPL, submission and participation post to the Individual Scorecard every evening.", "Banking Domain Use Case": "Banking customer churn — problem framing exercise", "AI Integration Touchpoint": "Use Claude to critique your problem framing — compare AI suggestions against peer feedback and identify what each one misses. Gemini used for background research on the banking brief.", "Core Topics — Live Session": "Straive context: banking & payments business model, client landscape · consulting vs engineering problem-solving mindsets · SMART KPIs · hypothesis-driven thinking · common-then-split architecture · HOW YOU ARE MEASURED: Individual Scorecard, daily tracking and the 360° evaluation framework walked through on Day 1 so every learner knows the bar from the outset", "Discipline Thread (Spec-First / Test-First)": "\\"Acceptance Criteria Before Approach\\" introduced BY NAME as the programme's operating principle. Every pod must write what a correct answer looks like before they are allowed to start solving — spec-first in plain language, before any tool is taught.", "SPL — Self-Paced Topic (not counted in hours)": "Banking & Payments 101 — industry primer, glossary, Straive org context"}
1636	73	5	2	Consulting & Engineering Mindsets + Repository Literacy	{"Day": "Day 2", "Hours": "8", "Difficulty": "⭐⭐", "Session Title": "Consulting & Engineering Mindsets + Repository Literacy", "Hands-On / Workshop": "Cross-functional pod exercise: MBA learners frame the business spec, Engineering learners frame the technical spec for the same banking problem, then trade and critique across discipline lines. Pods map their problem onto the data lifecycle and name who owns each stage. REPOSITORY SET-UP (45 min): every learner activates their GitLab account, clones the programme repository, commits the Day 1 problem statement and Day 2 spec with a written commit message, and confirms the commit appears in the history. Both tracks — the MBA cohort commits documents exactly as Engineering commits code.", "Assessment / Assignment": "Pod submission: paired business + technical spec for one banking scenario, peer-reviewed against a rubric. GATE: the spec must be committed to the learner's repository with a meaningful commit message — a first, low-stakes rehearsal of the repository discipline that becomes mandatory on Day 14.", "Banking Domain Use Case": "Digital onboarding friction — joint spec exercise", "AI Integration Touchpoint": "Compare a Claude-generated problem frame against the pod's own — identify the gaps the AI missed. Gemini used for market and competitor context.", "Core Topics — Live Session": "Decomposing ambiguous briefs · MECE structuring for technical and business contexts · spec-first thinking — why both disciplines benefit from writing the spec before building · THE DATA LIFECYCLE as the shared mental map for the next 15 days: source system → model → warehouse → pipeline → insight → decision · REPOSITORY LITERACY (light touch, 45 min, NEW): why version control exists and what problem it solves · repository, commit, branch and merge request explained in plain language for both tracks · why every piece of work in this programme is versioned and reviewed rather than emailed · what \\"main is protected\\" means and why. This is orientation only — the full Git & GitLab session, with branching strategies, merge conflicts, repository management and change management, is Day 14.", "Discipline Thread (Spec-First / Test-First)": "Reinforces Day 1: pods peer-review each other's \\"acceptance criteria\\" from the prior day before starting today's spec exercise. From today the commit message carries the same discipline in miniature — every commit must say what changed and why, which is the habit the Day 14 merge-request description formalises.", "SPL — Self-Paced Topic (not counted in hours)": "Intro to Spec-First Thinking — short primer for non-engineers · Version Control in 20 Minutes — repository literacy primer"}
